---
title: 100% Hydration Bread
description: This is the recipe for the bread I make nearly every day.
servings: 4
prep time: 480 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
total time: 500 minutes
notes: notes: notes: I use 12.5% protein bread flour for this.
---

Place #Mixing Bowl{} on #digital scale{}. Weigh @Water{350%g}, @Salt{8%g}, and @Yeast{8%g} into the bowl. Mix with #whisk until frothy. Weigh @Flour{350%g} into #Mixing Bowl{}. Mix with #Spatula until all of the @Flour is wet. Scrape the sides of the #Mixing Bowl{}, so there is one mass of dough. Put the #Mixing Bowl{} Cover on the bowl.

Refrigerate for at least 8 hours. I've tested up to 2 days, I haven't tested beyond that.

Pour @Olive Oil{5%ml} into #Bread Pan{}. Use a #pastry brush{} to spread it around the pan.

Remove #Mixing Bowl{} from #refrigerator. Uncover #Mixing Bowl{}. Use a wet Flexible #bench scraper{}, or a wet stiff #Spatula to release the dough from the #Mixing Bowl{}. I go around the edges in a circle, then under the dough on the final section, rewetting after each scrape. Pour the dough from the #Mixing Bowl{} into the Oiled #Bread Pan{}. Scrape any dough that sticks into the Oiled #Bread Pan{}. Cover the #Bread Pan{} with a #sheet pan{}, and place somewhere warm. ~{30%minutes}

Preheat oven to Max Temperature. Most days it takes between 30-45 minutes for the dough to raise to double the size of when you put it in the #Bread Pan{}. ~{15%minutes}

Once your oven is preheated, and the dough has doubled in size, bake for approximately 20 minutes. ~{20%minutes}

Check your bread. If the crust isn't dark enough, use the timer to check it again in 2 minutes. ~{2%minutes}
